14	// End-to-end regression for the member-fault precedence rule through the two
15	// real commands. A record that carries BOTH an unknown and a duplicated field
16	// must fail with a precise reason — and the first-reported problem differs by
17	// source even though both sources reject the record:
18	//
19	//   - a record read from the registry file names the duplicate first;
20	//   - a record read from the import manifest names the first anomaly in
21	//     source order (so an unknown field ahead of the repeat stays reported).
22	//
23	// Every failure must keep the source file path, the 1-based record position
24	// (here 2, after a legal record 1), the exact decoded field name and the
25	// batch id (trimmed for the manifest, verbatim for the registry), print no
26	// success output, leave the existing registry byte-for-byte untouched, and
27	// never write the read-only manifest.
